E0 MF >= E0 exact always (Rayleigh-Ritz). Symmetric MF gap/exact ranges 1.01 to ~1e6 (no constant);
broken MF predicts 0 where exact > 0. Neither MF gap gives two-sided control of E1 - E0.

== E. Covariant-gauge one-loop tadpole (4-gluon vertex) at zero momentum ==
D_{rs}(k) = [(delta - k k/k^2) + xi k k/k^2]/k^2; angular average of k_r k_s/k^2 = delta_rs/d
   xi    Pi_00 / (g^2 C_A I)    (d-1+xi)(d-1)/d
  0.0                 2.2495             2.2500
  0.5                 2.6248             2.6250
  1.0                 3.0000             3.0000
  3.0                 4.5010             4.5000
Hartree mass^2 from the quartic vertex is linear in xi: Feynman/Landau = 4/3 in d = 4.
A physical pole mass is xi-independent (Nielsen identities), so this 'mass' is not one.

